cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use TaskVerse or its planning engine in research, please cite it as below.
type: software
title: 'TaskVerse: a task management platform with a reproducible planning and flow-analytics engine'
authors:
  - family-names: Praveen
    given-names: Satvik
    email: satvikpraveen707@gmail.com
repository-code: https://github.com/SatvikPraveen/TaskVerse
license: MIT
version: 2.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-03
keywords:
  - task scheduling
  - weighted shortest job first
  - earliest deadline first
  - critical path method
  - monte carlo forecasting
  - flow metrics
  - typescript
abstract: >-
  TaskVerse pairs a conventional task-management application (Express, MongoDB,
  React) with a pure, dependency-free planning engine that implements
  dependency graphs, the Critical Path Method, six prioritisation policies
  (FIFO, static priority, SPT, EDF, WSJF, Eisenhower), a non-preemptive list
  scheduler, bootstrap Monte Carlo completion forecasting and Kanban flow
  metrics. A seeded benchmark harness evaluates the policies on synthetic
  workloads and the calibration of the forecaster, and the same engine powers
  the application's planning and analytics endpoints.
